    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0153" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1840: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-12T22:00:00-04:00">September 12, 1939—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>930. Your 1582, September 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d121-f1"/> The final
                    text of the Agenda has been communicated to the diplomatic representatives here
                    of the countries with officers on the Committee.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d121-f2"
                    /> As a courtesy please inform Ambassador Le Breton and Count Limburg-Stirum of
                    the change in Paragraph Six and repeat Department’s 857, September 8, noon, to
                    the American Embassy at Paris with the request that Bérenger be notified of the
                    change and to the American Legation, Bern, for the information of Lobo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d121-f1" n="77" xml:id="d121-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d121-f2" n="78" xml:id="d121-f2-content">
                <p>The notes to the Argentine, Brazilian, British, and French Embassies, and the
                    Netherlands Legation, were dated September 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
